codemap 8
path gfx-renderer
kind layer
author ai
group render
note The GPU side: one wgpu pipeline that draws everything the app ever draws as textured, coloured quads out of a single atlas. The atlas holds every glyph at every pixel size in use, rasterised on demand by fontdue, plus a white patch in the corner that solid fills sample - which is why a rectangle, a line, a bezier and a run of text are all the same draw call with the same shader. Positions are whole physical pixels and the sampler is nearest, so text is never scaled or sampled between pixels; a different zoom is a different font size, not a transform. Clipping is a scissor rectangle, and the frame is cut into commands wherever the clip changes, so a deeply nested tree is still one vertex buffer.

